  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It builds a forest from a seeded RNG, so the layout is the same on every load. It has a 260×260 ground plane and 10,000 instances in three instanced draws: 8,000 trunks (cylinders), 8,000 canopies (cones) and 2,000 rocks (squashed spheres). The 8,000 trees count as one trunk plus one canopy each. Canopies and rocks each get a per-instance HSL colour over a white base material. One shadow-casting directional light, a hemisphere light and exponential fog (density 0.004) are set up. The camera is an orbit camera with `autoRotate` 0.08 rad/s, positioned at [0,75,115] with near 20 and far 450. I set a larger far plane because the default of 100 would clip the forest from that distance. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set on the second `onFrame` callback, after the first frame has drawn. `typecheck` passes. I did not run `vite build` or load the page in a browser, so I haven't seen the rendered frame or checked that the shadows cover the whole forest.",
